<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lake Matano</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lake Matano is a lake in the highlands of South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulawesi">Sulawesi</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, and at about 590 metres one of the deepest lakes in the world. The surrounding hills hold rich deposits of iron and nickel ore, which made the area an early source of iron for Luwu and other kingdoms of Sulawesi. Its waters are home to many fish and snails found nowhere else.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lake-matano.jpg" alt="Lake Matano" width="270" height="360" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Isuru Senevi (talk) · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Matano_Sunset.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
